 task performance</article-title><source>J Neurochem</source><year>2005</year><volume>95</volume><fpage>848</fpage><lpage>857</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16135079</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1471-4159.2005.03427.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lim</surname><given-names>SY</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoshiba</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Moriguchi</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Salem</surname><given-names>N</given-names><suffix>Jr.</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>N-3 fatty acid deficiency induced by a modified artificial rearing method leads to poorer performance in spatial learning tasks</article-title><source>Pediatr Res</source><year>2005</year><volume>58</volume><fpage>741</fpage><lpage>748</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16189203</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1203/01.PDR.0000180547.46725.CC</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moriguchi</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Lim</surname><given-names>SY</given-names></name><name><surname>Greiner</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Lefkowitz</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Loewke</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoshiba</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Salem</surname><given-names>N</given-names><suffix>Jr.</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>Effects of an n-3-deficient diet on brain, retina, and liver fatty acyl composition in artificially reared rats</article-title><source>J Lipid Res</source><year>2004</year><volume>45</volume><fpage>1437</fpage><lpage>1445</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15175358</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1194/jlr.M400087-JLR200</pub-id></citation></ref><ref 